 "notes": "Curve traced from the vector graphics of Fig. 4b: the boundary of the blue-shaded region, i.e. the 95% CL exclusion from the 100-s-per-run scan over 8.3-744 feV (the paper's continuous excluded region). The plotted limit is a rapidly oscillating jagged curve; each reported point is the median of the curve within an ~8 feV mass bin (local dips are up to ~2x lower, peaks ~2x higher). The paper also reports deeper 5-h limits, but only in 100 narrow (0.15 feV wide) windows, reaching g_aNN = 2.9e-9 GeV^-1 at 67.5 feV; that discrete comb (Fig. 4b red) is ~10x below the reported continuous curve and is described in the caption as 'advanced sensitivity'. Axis calibration cross-checked against tick marks and the quoted 5-h value. Conversion: paper quotes g_aNN in GeV^-1 for the gradient coupling (supplement Eq. J7, H = g_aNN sqrt(2 hbar^3 c rho) sin(2 pi nu t) v.I_N); converted to the canonical dimensionless coupling via the 2m_N rule, g_an = 2 x 0.9396 GeV x g_aNN. 129Xe spin is neutron-dominated, so the nucleon coupling is reported as AxionNeutron (proton set to zero). rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed by the paper.",
